                "entry_id": "7f1900be-9f45-309a-bbbe-5a214163b794",
                "word": "Shaanxi",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "270792e6-c2b1-31c5-b38e-6349a8ef4d55",
                        "entry_id": "7f1900be-9f45-309a-bbbe-5a214163b794",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Province au centre de la Chine, dont le chef-lieu est Xi’an."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07da6b64-61fe-42e7-bcd5-c1312ca8784a",
                                "sense_id": "270792e6-c2b1-31c5-b38e-6349a8ef4d55",
                                "text": "L’explosion s’est produite dans la ville de Xinmin, dans la province de Shaanxi, et a endommagé des dizaines d’immeubles, dont un hôpital."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cee0796b-dea8-4329-b540-00d9b6cf1172",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f1900be-9f45-309a-bbbe-5a214163b794",
                        "source_sense_id": "270792e6-c2b1-31c5-b38e-6349a8ef4d55",
                        "target_lang_word": "Shaanxi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Shaanxi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                        "entry_id": "06f93dad-f2e7-34bc-8bdc-9f93ddb4fff7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A province of China, including the Wei River valley and the fertile southern half of the Ordos Loop, comprising much of the Loess Plateau. Capital: Xi'an."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a72cf06-90df-496e-a245-025f078a39f6",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "The fact, therefore, that the Tae pings, when they raised the siege of Hwae king on the 1st September marched westwards by it into Shan se, shows that the Imperial forces were strong enough to prevent their descent by the Wei river."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79b57f70-5c5a-4fa2-a842-75a939690f7c",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "Under the Pinyin system, two neighboring provinces of northern China are both spelled \"Shanxi\". In this special case, one of the provinces is now spelled \"Shaanxi\", to indicate a different tone in the first syllable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5b500fe-ed52-40eb-8454-9e14f2015749",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "Three pieces of paper which may date back to between 73 and 49 BC were recently found in Fufeng county, Shaanxi province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3a44096-497c-491c-bd91-fca480a34ee3",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "HUANG DI, the legendary Yellow Emperor to whom is attributed the founding of the Chinese nation about 2000 B.C., is said to have been buried on the loess plateau. There is a tomb in Shaanxi province’s Huangling county which has long been honored as his."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b62929c0-f707-4c52-9d9b-7fd17967e62d",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "Relevant new discoveries in China, not yet described, include polybranchiaspids and hanyangaspids which were recently (1981-82) recovered from an Early Silurian formation in western Hunan Province of south China, and in southern Shaanxi Province, west China."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dad62f65-be6a-4c39-84cb-25e60c24e9e3",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "\"Archeologists drew almost a complete blank in their search of the inner tomb,\" the official New China News Agency said Saturday in a report of excavations at the tomb site, thought to be between 2,200 and 2,800 years old. The site is in Fengxiang County of Shaanxi Province, about 90 miles west of the ancient Yellow River capital of Xian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "722f6465-171b-4bfc-8e1f-fd0bdb839366",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "Twenty one people were killed in China after the roof of a coal mine collapsed in Lijiagou, in the central province Shaanxi, state media reported on Sunday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb88d632-e7fd-4456-837a-cd5073611d82",
                                                "sense_id": "f1afcf6b-3d4d-3e4e-93f2-38238a45f848",
                                                "text": "Zhao Xiaoqing, a 28-year-old woman from northern China's Shaanxi province, thought her date in mid-December with a young man living in a different city would be a one-day affair where she would also get to know his family."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
